WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:03.980
Second Time
Monday
October 23rd

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:08.480
Hi, Oka Eri.

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:11.440
What a nice morning, don't you think?

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.320
Hey there.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.240
It's a terrible morning, honestly.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.160
The middle school is the other way.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.200
Where are you going?

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.910
Nowhere.

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:23.160
A villain doesn't show up at school.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:26.630
I don't think a villain would
cooperate with the government either.

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:29.670
You're on your way to help Urachi, aren't you?

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.840
None of your business.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:33.420
Oka Eri.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.260
I want you to side with me, not him.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.100
You don't understand a thing, do you?

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.100
What I want to see is how you lose!

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:44.140
Do you know what Urachi is planning to do?

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:47.730
As long as I win, it doesn't matter at all.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:51.860
Urachi is trying to rid Sakurada of all abilities.

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:57.200
Everyone will forget about them,
and Sakurada will become an ordinary peaceful town.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.990
That's Urachi Masamune's plan.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.200
I want to prevent that.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.290
I want to protect the abilities.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:04.870
That's why...

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:06.210
Let me ask you this.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:11.800
Oka Eri, please help me.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:45.520
What?

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:48.850
Do you think I'll help you
just because you lowered your head?

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:50.100
Of course.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:52.730
You will help me.

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:54.440
Why?

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:57.740
Silly question. Because that's your goal.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:01.070
Oka Eri, you said you wanted to win.

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:03.450
You said you wanted to prove my weaknesses.

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:04.990
Of course! So—

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:08.160
So you will help me.

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:09.620
What?

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:12.630
Listen, I used a reset.

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:13.670
And?

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:17.050
I was completely cornered by you and Urachi.

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:20.840
I utterly lost, and ran away with a reset.

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:23.220
And now I've come to you for help.

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:25.470
You know what it means, Oka Eri?

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:27.180
What I'm saying is

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:30.140
"I give up, so help me."

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:31.440
What?

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:34.020
I've never seen such a proud surrender!

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.400
Okay, Oka Eri. Help me.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.650
That'll be your victory.

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:40.780
You're doing all of this on purpose.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:45.870
If you pretended to be the same
as two years ago, I'd help you.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:47.030
Isn't that what you thought?

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:51.080
This is an honest surrender,
from the bottom of my heart.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:53.620
The purest declaration of my defeat.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.460
Even now,

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:58.210
I still believe what I did two years ago was wrong.

00:03:58.210 --> 00:03:58.880
But I—

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:01.720
But for now, I'll accept defeat.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:06.600
I'll admit that I've gotten weak in the
past two years, just like you're claiming.

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:16.360
So? What will you make me do?

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:21.740
Sorry for the wait.

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:28.450
Okay, let's start.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:31.290
Start? Start what?

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:35.290
The meeting to decide Sakurada's future.

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:38.290
Second Time
Monday, 9:30 AM
October 23rd

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:49.010
Hm, so it <i>is</i> different.

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:52.310
Before the reset, today at 9:30 AM,

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:56.770
there was a traffic accident caused
by the first ability rampage case.

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:58.150
So we failed?

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:00.530
We did.

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:02.610
He must have done something.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:06.410
Oka Eri didn't show up either.

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:09.450
That's another change after the reset.

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:12.910
I wonder what Asai is trying to do.

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:16.250
Doesn't he want to protect Sakurada's abilities?

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:17.880
Of course.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:18.630
But you see...

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:20.420
How will he do it?

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:22.380
If he's not a complete fool,

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:26.590
he should be aware that it's impossible
to keep standing in my way.

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:29.010
I don't think he's a fool.

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:30.850
Then there's only one possibility.

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:34.020
If he's not a fool, he's a genius.

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:37.980
He must have found a way to win against me.

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:39.860
Some way...

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:42.730
That's all.

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:44.780
Any questions?

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:52.830
Ukawa,

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:55.500
I just want to talk with Urachi.

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:58.210
I want both of us to speak from our hearts.

00:05:58.210 --> 00:06:00.710
In a way we can shake hands after.

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:03.500
I don't want to fight.

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:06.170
I want a discussion where
we can exchange opinions.

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:10.550
I know that you're both just and
level-headed in your world-saving.

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:12.970
So now that you've learned everything,

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:15.430
if you still want to side with Urachi,
I won't stop you.

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:20.270
But Urachi doesn't leave any room for negotiations,
he decides everything by himself.

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:24.860
So I want you to watch me closely, Ukawa.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:27.780
I'm quite certain you'll deem my actions righteous.

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:31.280
Will you agree with that or not?

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:34.160
Please see for yourself.

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:47.510
Hi.

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:50.010
It's been a while, Urachi.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:51.760
Has it?

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:55.260
Didn't we meet a day or two ago?

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:58.140
I've used a reset, though.

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:00.980
The last time we met was last month.

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:03.810
I wonder, why have you reset?

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:05.230
That much should be obvious.

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:07.400
Something unpleasant happened, that's all.

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:09.400
I see. What exactly?

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:13.370
There was a traffic accident, for instance.

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:15.830
And abilities disappeared from Sakurada.

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:20.370
So you reset and prevented
the accident from happening.

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:22.170
The cause of the accident

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:25.670
was a little girl using her ability without realizing it.

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:27.340
Urachi.

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:30.930
Do you know what kind of ability the girl had?

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:32.050
No.

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:34.930
Isn't it written in your notebook?

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:36.680
The ability she used

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:40.730
made people unable to turn towards her.

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:44.860
As a result, a driver who couldn't
look forward caused an accident.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:47.070
The user must've been really shy.

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:49.990
The girl tripped.

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:53.820
A sidewalk tile was cracked and her foot got stuck.

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:58.040
She must've used her ability because she was embarrassed about tripping in front of people.

00:07:58.040 --> 00:07:59.250
I see.

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:03.170
So preventing the girl from tripping
also prevented the accident.

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:03.960
Yes.

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:07.380
I moved some flowers over the crack this morning.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:11.470
The crack she was supposed to trip over later.

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:13.050
Asai,

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:15.850
do you realize what you've done?

00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:17.930
I prevented an unfortunate accident.

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:20.020
That's certainly admirable.

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:23.600
But you're smart enough
to understand that's not all, right?

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:28.520
If there was a problem before your reset
big enough to warrant erasing all abilities,

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:31.780
you should've reported that to the Bureau.

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:33.860
That's true.

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:38.200
But instead, you erased the
Bureau's decision with a reset.

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:40.040
That's against the law.

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:42.080
It's a crime you can't talk your way out of.

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:44.750
Right back at you, Urachi.

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:47.840
You intentionally caused a problem.

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:51.710
You set everything up so the Bureau
would make the wrong decision.

00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:54.720
That's also a crime you can't talk your way out of.

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:56.720
Isn't that just your guess?

00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:59.430
What if I had an objective basis for that?

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:00.720
Then I'd love to hear it.

00:09:01.220 --> 00:09:03.850
There's a girl called Souma Sumire.

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:07.310
She died two years ago,
but came back to life this summer.

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:08.230
And?

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:10.690
She's a future-seer.

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:16.110
I see. You're so mean.

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:20.660
Clairvoyance is the most highly
regarded ability in Sakurada.

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:23.870
If there's a girl possessing this ability,

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:27.330
even you shouldn't keep that information secret.

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:29.500
But you never told the Bureau.

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:34.050
Because if the Witch had a successor, it'd become
more difficult for you to confuse the Bureau.

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:35.720
You don't have any proof.

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:38.970
Now I do. Because I told you about her.

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:42.520
If you keep Souma's existence
secret from the Bureau,

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:46.480
it's a crime you can't talk your
way out of that I have proof of.

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:52.070
Urachi, why don't we talk face to face?

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:53.530
Let's meet, then.

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:55.820
What do you want to talk about, though?

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:59.570
I think we're both misunderstanding each other.

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:01.370
I want to clear things up.

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:02.910
I see.

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:05.620
Let's meet in one hour, then.

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:07.790
That soon?

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:08.870
Is that a problem?

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:11.540
<i>He's making sure we can't prepare for it...</i>

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:14.130
I'd rather meet tonight or tomorrow.

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:15.510
Do you not have time?

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:18.510
I don't. I'm a busy man.

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:21.970
If you can't meet me now,
I won't have time for a while.

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:24.600
I see.

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:28.140
Let's meet in an hour, at eleven.

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:30.900
I'll send the location to Index.

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:32.940
Sure.

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:34.650
I'll be waiting.

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:38.280
I'm going to meet Urachi.

00:10:38.610 --> 00:10:42.030
It doesn't seem like it'll just be a simple nice chat,

00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:45.040
and we can't save for another nine hours.

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:48.410
Haruki, I'm in a very bad situation right now.

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:49.960
Will you help me?

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:52.040
Yes, of course.

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:53.040
Thanks.

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:56.840
Everyone, please take a while to think.

00:10:56.840 --> 00:10:59.300
I'll leave for around thirty minutes.

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:02.470
If you think abilities should exist in Sakurada,

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:04.010
please stay in this room.

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:07.270
I'll be back in thirty minutes, then.

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:18.030
Kei. Don't you want to convince them?

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:20.110
There's no need to.

00:11:20.110 --> 00:11:23.410
When I used clairvoyance inside the picture,

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:25.780
I learned a bit about the future.

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:26.790
Does that mean...

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:31.250
I only pretended to give those five a choice.

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:33.460
I know what they're going to choose.

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:35.630
That's why I needed a break.

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:38.130
No matter how honest the words,

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:41.880
if you voice them only after
learning the answer, it's like a lie.

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:45.050
I'm glad.

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:49.430
You always seem to be forcing yourself.

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:54.520
I'm glad you took a break for once.

00:11:56.610 --> 00:12:00.110
<i>It's thanks to Souma that
I'm able to talk to Haruki again.</i>

00:12:00.650 --> 00:12:04.990
<i>That's... That means the world to me.</i>

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:09.500
<i>The one message Souma risked her life to deliver</i>

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:12.120
<i>protected all I hold dear.</i>

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:28.260
Is that the room?

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:36.150
It's nice to see you again, Urachi, Index.

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:37.610
Oh, and Kagaya.

00:12:39.730 --> 00:12:41.740
You have guards outside of the room?

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:47.160
No, his only job is to open and close the door.

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:48.450
Would you like to sing?

00:12:48.450 --> 00:12:52.830
We can't sing on duty in the Bureau.

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:54.160
Really?

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:57.750
Asai, let's keep this discussion efficient.

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:00.340
I'll get to the main topic, then.

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:04.130
I'm thinking about preserving
the abilities in this town.

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:07.340
It'd be a shame to throw away those prayers
that are answered with miracles.

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:12.470
I, on the other hand, think abilities
should all disappear from this world.

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:17.310
This fake hope they give only creates tragedies,
like a devil's power.

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:20.020
Our opinions are polar opposites.

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:21.280
That's true.

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:25.200
If there's no room for a compromise,
we can only do as we please now.

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:26.490
I wonder.

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:30.240
Urachi, don't you think erasing abilities

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:33.750
simply means you want to have
absolute control over all the abilities?

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:35.500
That's true.

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:38.250
I agree in that matter.

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:39.330
And?

00:13:39.330 --> 00:13:42.000
I'm saying that we're quite similar.

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:45.260
I'm also planning to control all abilities.

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:50.300
I can prove it's possible to control all of this town's
abilities without making people forget about them.

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:53.600
A single human shouldn't have all that power.

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:54.930
I'm aware of that.

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:58.270
Right now, they're not being
controlled by the Bureau's staff,

00:13:58.270 --> 00:14:00.480
but by the Bureau's system itself.

00:14:00.810 --> 00:14:01.900
Yeah.

00:14:01.900 --> 00:14:04.690
The Bureau doesn't allow dictatorship.

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:06.200
But, Urachi,

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:08.360
if the system of the Bureau is absolute,

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:11.200
and even the people there can't oppose it,

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:13.620
doesn't that make it the same as dictatorship?

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:17.580
You're absolutely right, Asai.

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:20.750
It's one of the main problems of the Bureau.

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:23.130
If there's an error in the system itself,

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:25.300
we can't deal with that in any way.

00:14:25.300 --> 00:14:27.840
It remains an error for eternity.

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:28.800
I can see that.

00:14:30.300 --> 00:14:32.970
Which means, if an ability user
is sacrificed to the system,

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:35.270
they cannot be saved in any way, can they?

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:38.190
In other words, the two ability
users that created the border

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:42.110
won't ever be saved due to how
the system of the Bureau works.

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:43.520
So you're saying, Asai,

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:47.900
that to resolve the problems created by
the Bureau being trapped in its own system,

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:50.360
you'll go as far as to become a dictator?

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:52.450
A ruler with a mind and a will

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:55.700
would create an environment free
of the errors of the current system.

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:57.620
That's more or less correct.

00:14:57.620 --> 00:14:59.500
I'd like to add one more thing, though.

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:00.500
What is it?

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:04.130
Even I can't fully trust myself.

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:06.000
I make mistakes sometimes.

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:08.590
What I consider right

00:15:08.590 --> 00:15:11.470
might become like one of
the system errors you speak of.

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:14.600
Yeah, it's perfectly normal to fear that.

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:17.720
That's where I want to ask you a favor, Urachi.

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:21.730
I need to be under someone's surveillance.

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:25.610
Not a system,
but a few people who do have emotions

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:27.570
should be watching over me.

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:30.200
I'm considering you to be one of them.

00:15:30.860 --> 00:15:34.240
Please. I'd like you to work with me.

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:39.540
Sure. It's a brilliant idea.

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:42.000
I'll fully support you.

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:53.220
He's my most trusted colleague.

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:56.810
I'm sure he'll help you as well.

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:08.730
What's wrong, Asai?

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:18.490
You don't want to shake his hand?

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:26.210
It'll be a pleasure to work with you, Kagaya.

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:32.970
This is the end.

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:37.220
No. It's the beginning.

00:16:40.310 --> 00:16:41.310
Director...

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:45.940
I can't remember how to use my ability.

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:55.610
Asai,

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:58.700
you seem to have a lot of amazing friends.

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:01.040
It's not a lot.

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:02.830
But you're right.

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:04.670
They're all such a great help.

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:08.750
It must feel great when everything
proceeds according to your plan, doesn't it?

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:10.670
It's not like that.

00:17:10.670 --> 00:17:13.550
You never looked me in the eyes properly.

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:15.010
But of course.

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:17.840
I'd never do something that risky.

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:19.640
When did you realize?

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:23.980
When you set up our meeting at a karaoke place.

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:26.350
I pretended not to notice,

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:29.360
but you needed to prepare a private room.

00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:32.190
Two adjacent rooms, in fact.

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:32.900
Yes.

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:36.280
You've gathered your friends in the other room.

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:37.950
Have I?

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:41.080
I sure hope they all consider me their friend.

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:44.960
One of them has an ability to manipulate memories.

00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:46.710
What triggers the ability

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:49.580
is looking someone in the eyes
for five seconds, was it?

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:50.540
Exactly.

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:52.420
She's a girl called Oka Eri.

00:17:52.420 --> 00:17:54.460
Another one can copy abilities.

00:17:54.460 --> 00:17:58.800
Thanks to him, you temporarily gained
the ability to manipulate memories.

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:00.350
That's Sakagami.

00:18:00.350 --> 00:18:04.390
But he can only copy an ability
for the time he's touching the target.

00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:07.440
Isn't there also someone
who can open a hole in the wall?

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:12.230
There's a hole in the sofa you're sitting on,
and they're touching your back from the other room.

00:18:12.230 --> 00:18:13.730
That's Murase.

00:18:13.730 --> 00:18:16.990
She's able to erase any object
or phenomenon for five minutes.

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:18.820
Thanks to the efforts of your friends,

00:18:18.820 --> 00:18:22.870
you temporarily gained the ability
to manipulate memories.

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:27.660
And so you made Kagaya
forget how to use his ability.

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:29.330
That's right.

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:32.750
You were planning to use it on me, weren't you?

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:37.840
You wanted to manipulate my memories
and force me to listen to you.

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:41.140
How uncivilized,
meddling with people's minds.

00:18:41.140 --> 00:18:42.680
But it's all pointless.

00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:44.970
Asai.

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:47.230
Your effort is all in vain.

00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:51.230
With my ability I can rewind the time of any object.

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:54.150
Rewinding Kagaya to just ten minutes ago

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:56.820
will make him remember how to use his ability.

00:18:57.900 --> 00:19:00.490
What just...

00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:02.120
See, he's back to normal.

00:19:02.780 --> 00:19:05.040
Let me repeat myself, Asai.

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:06.450
This is the end.

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:08.040
The end?

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:09.790
You don't understand a thing.

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:12.080
This is not even the beginning.

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:16.550
Why do you think I'm continuing
this pointless conversation?

00:19:16.550 --> 00:19:23.140
Actually, why do you think I didn't warn
Kagaya despite realizing your trap?

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:25.760
It's because I suspected all of it.

00:19:25.760 --> 00:19:28.430
The moment you used your abilities against us,

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:31.190
your defeat was assured.

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:36.440
Asai Kei,

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:41.110
you have used an ability against a Bureau
employee to interfere with their duties.

00:19:41.110 --> 00:19:44.990
Under the law of the Bureau,
you will now be restrained.

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:56.880
Why do you think you were
the only one who was buying time?

00:19:57.460 --> 00:20:03.260
You made such a silly mistake, I can't believe
Souma Sumire had such a hard time opposing you.

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:09.640
I made up my mind two years ago that I'd
oppose the Bureau with all my power, if necessary.

00:20:09.640 --> 00:20:12.640
But I wouldn't want to win that way.

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:16.060
Urachi, now everything will begin.

00:20:38.380 --> 00:20:40.630
Was that Ukawa Sasane?

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:41.840
That's right.

00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:44.840
Within one minute,
she can create whatever she imagines.

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:47.930
I haven't been on a slide since elementary school.

00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:49.430
Hey, Kei.

00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:52.430
Who is that man in an expensive looking suit?

00:20:52.430 --> 00:20:53.810
God,

00:20:53.810 --> 00:20:56.650
I can't believe I'm helping
one of my students skip school.

00:20:56.650 --> 00:20:58.020
It's unthinkable.

00:20:58.020 --> 00:21:00.150
It's because we're in an unthinkable situation.

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:03.030
You, driver.

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:05.200
You're Tsushima Shintarou?

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:06.910
That's right.

00:21:07.620 --> 00:21:09.120
This is crazy.

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:12.700
Why are you using someone
from the Bureau as your driver?

00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:16.290
I don't know anyone else with a license.

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:18.420
Are you serious?

00:21:18.420 --> 00:21:20.340
What in the world is happening?

00:21:20.340 --> 00:21:21.840
This is Urachi Masamune.

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:25.590
He's the director of the Bureau's
countermeasures department.

00:21:25.590 --> 00:21:26.640
What?!

00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:28.930
Nice to meet you, Tsushima.

00:21:28.930 --> 00:21:31.810
I've heard you're an excellent
member of the Bureau.

00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:33.810
I'm surprised.

00:21:33.810 --> 00:21:35.190
I am as well.

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:37.310
Kei, can you explain yourself?

00:21:37.310 --> 00:21:40.070
I entrapped and kidnapped him.

00:21:40.070 --> 00:21:43.240
Spare me the jokes, I want to hear the truth.

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:44.360
This is the truth.

00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:48.240
I am currently being kidnapped by Asai.

00:21:48.740 --> 00:21:50.240
And, Tsushima...

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:53.290
You're his accomplice.

00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:57.500
Next Episode

00:21:57.500 --> 00:21:59.580
Do you really think you can convince me?

00:21:59.580 --> 00:22:00.670
Let's take a classic hostage.

00:22:00.670 --> 00:22:02.050
He got rid of you.

00:22:02.050 --> 00:22:02.960
You have to accept all the despair and trouble!

00:22:02.960 --> 00:22:05.050
Stop! Stop, please!
You have to accept all the despair and trouble!

00:22:05.050 --> 00:22:06.840
and live without turning
your eyes away from reality!

00:22:06.840 --> 00:22:10.180
You're the one turning your eyes away from reality.

00:22:17.440 --> 00:22:21.400
On such a cold dark sky of grey

00:22:23.690 --> 00:22:27.610
Rises the sun, which breathes life into it

00:22:29.700 --> 00:22:33.870
A scenery so plain and so mundane

00:22:34.160 --> 00:22:43.460
And yet it seems to break my heart, it's so dear to me

00:22:44.340 --> 00:22:45.130
As the time never stops passing by

00:22:45.130 --> 00:22:47.920
As the time never stops passing by

00:22:47.920 --> 00:22:50.300
You get lost while searching for

00:22:50.300 --> 00:22:54.180
Pure like the rays of a morning star

00:22:54.180 --> 00:22:57.100
What we all yearn for the most

00:22:57.100 --> 00:23:00.520
In what colors bliss is dyed

00:23:00.650 --> 00:23:03.150
Struggling against all your past mistakes

00:23:03.150 --> 00:23:06.190
At last from the answer you found kindness fills your heart

00:23:06.780 --> 00:23:09.360
More beautiful than anything you know

00:23:09.360 --> 00:23:12.990
And you find it behind a dark veil of sadness

00:23:12.990 --> 00:23:15.490
If I closed my eyes and stopped my thoughts

00:23:15.490 --> 00:23:17.250
If it were so simple to just

00:23:17.250 --> 00:23:20.250
Lock your own heart

00:23:20.250 --> 00:23:23.380
How lovely life would be

00:23:23.380 --> 00:23:28.630
But I believe you have the key

00:23:29.420 --> 00:23:34.970
To let my soul be free
